pr_body:
Reindexing requires `ignore_unavailable` search option to be set on request to execute reindex from remote - to be able to reference remote index in a format **cluster_name:index_name**
https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/2e6834ad1103f7eab2e5a9cf2dcb5816ec4d2d17/server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/cluster/metadata/IndexNameExpressionResolver.java#L1612-L1622

Unfortunately [Reindex API](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/docs-reindex.html#docs-reindex-api-query-params) does not have `ignore_unavailable` among supported query parameters. In the same time there is cluster level settings `cluster.remote.<cluster_name>.skip_unavailable` which allows check if remote cluster is configured to skip unavailable indices.

This PR checks if CCS/CCR is enabled and modifies request object if there is `skip_unavailable` flag is present.
Both re-index request formats are supported now

Request 1:
```
curl -X POST "localhost:19200/_reindex?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
{
  "source": {
        "remote": {
                "host": "http://172.18.0.2:9200"
        },
    "index": "my-index-000001"
  },
  "dest": {
    "index": "my-index-000001"
  }
}
'
```

Request 2:
```
curl -X POST "localhost:19200/_reindex?pretty" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d'
{
  "source": {
    "index": "cluster0:my-index-000001"
  },
  "dest": {
    "index": "my-index-000001"
  }
}
'
```

Closes #89120

